      "created_at": "2026-06-15T02:32:59Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-06-15T02:32:59Z",
      "body": "As soon as this flexcomp model penetrates the floor, the programme crashes. Error message:\n```bash\nWARNING: Too many contacts. The arena memory is full, increase arena memory allocation.(ncon = 22287) Time = 0.1380.\nERROR: findEdges: no tree found for constraint 0\n```\nAlso, once a relatively complex model is loaded, the simulation frame rate drops to 40fps or even 5fps. In my work environment, we\u2019ll probably still need to rely on Coal\u2019s collision algorithm to meet our requirements.\nBut thank you all the same, @quagla, for letting me know about `rigid flex`. Thank you.\ud83d\ude0a",
