      "updated_at": "2026-06-16T01:55:07Z",
      "body": "Whenever this object penetrates a static object (such as the floor or something else), the error `ERROR: findEdges: no tree found for constraint 0` is reported. However, this is likely not a major issue, as normal simulations should not permit penetration either.\n\nThat said, ordinary objects (non-flexcomp) do not cause the simulation to crash even if penetration occurs.",
